        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                "word": "non-dit",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a0f5d345-18e5-49cc-a451-02c3a0545d97",
                        "entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "non-dits"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                        "entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chose qui ne se dit pas, trop évidente ou taboue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd1267ae-d034-468a-8d16-157bfef06480",
                                "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                                "text": "Il faut pourtant voir de quoi il s’agit : est-ce d’une absence de politique linguistique ou d’une stratégie de non-dit ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0c8d016-2a51-4ed3-8ac6-1ea9f9115562",
                                "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                                "text": "Mais pour l'heure, tout le monde fait comme si le problème n'existait pas. Ce non-dit est dangereux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6926aac0-eaa5-47a7-a9a2-65fcecd1374a",
                                "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                                "text": "Tout livre, pour trouver grâce à ses yeux, doit savoir préserver son lot de non-dits, de secrets, et faire confiance au lecteur. Tout dévoiler, c'est priver celui-ci de sa propre découverte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57d9eccf-f207-4013-9767-0834b33d01c3",
                                "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                                "text": "Le corsetage un peu plat de la justesse figurative gagne un volume captivant en débouchant sur le non-dit, le non-peint, les insondables possibilités de rêver sur les choses qui s’échappent, les fascinantes vies qui ne sont pas finies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f4fd14d-96c2-46fc-b02d-c36f618f1630",
                                "sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                                "text": "Il y avait un non-dit, un sous-texte invisible dans ce dialogue, se dit-elle..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c895a4aa-5090-448a-963c-06026381ffbe",
                        "source_entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                        "target_lang_word": "thing left unsaid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a034ba53-c0be-461b-9e32-56544381a243",
                        "source_entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                        "target_lang_word": "thing left unspoken",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d231c6ff-f479-4b8a-bdad-97b1ae43f025",
                        "source_entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                        "target_lang_word": "unsaid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unsaid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5f9da6d-064b-3b57-a072-e15fe47a57f6",
                                        "entry_id": "ec158a3a-2ff6-39ec-bb8a-4332c85b5d26",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of unsay"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb5b1584-9d96-4242-af08-19b43b26829d",
                                                "sense_id": "a5f9da6d-064b-3b57-a072-e15fe47a57f6",
                                                "text": "Once there, she makes good use of her time, and retakes all those said letters; considering, perhaps, that what is said may be unsaid, but what is written remains in evidence against you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "unsaid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b196632-1b67-3887-bf11-03ff13bfb541",
                                        "entry_id": "29b3a671-b870-3a86-a962-843c0c913472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unspoken."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17fdcec7-7c61-4ff8-ac56-7014aa2d5873",
                                                "sense_id": "9b196632-1b67-3887-bf11-03ff13bfb541",
                                                "text": "We discussed the terms, but the methods were left unsaid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ae70302-adb7-4d84-a466-cda5dd81ca23",
                                                "sense_id": "9b196632-1b67-3887-bf11-03ff13bfb541",
                                                "text": "Informal techniques, if properly written, can be quite readable and comprehensible; unfortunately, it is easy to leave unsaid details that must be specified, or to misgeneralise and produce inconsistencies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "453a228c-ee6f-4da0-b475-18f99f870599",
                        "source_entry_id": "123b049c-3f95-30f5-9f87-d35fa2be97ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abc52e3-6ea8-376c-bf17-af5fd940268a",
                        "target_lang_word": "unspoken",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unspoken",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b8a7a45-4aef-36dd-b9f7-34911653bd7c",
                                        "entry_id": "cab4b411-0cbf-3e40-9176-fe8e57ae7e1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not spoken; not said."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "postpositional",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb0c783b-2243-3f96-aa39-1d50252b510a",
                                        "entry_id": "cab4b411-0cbf-3e40-9176-fe8e57ae7e1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not formally articulated or stated; implicit or understood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "postpositional",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22db529c-37e7-4fd9-89fe-2209fef2530a",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c783b-2243-3f96-aa39-1d50252b510a",
                                                "text": "The unspoken rule is to start a new pot of coffee when it is empty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddba325e-9f2c-4040-b959-9041e5ccabdf",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c783b-2243-3f96-aa39-1d50252b510a",
                                                "text": "I don't think we could ever have a good parent-son relationship as long as there is something as important as this that I'm hiding from you, and you (probably) are wondering about vaguely, but everything remains on a silent unspoken level."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be8a2030-de7c-43cb-a218-a26e25b813e0",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c783b-2243-3f96-aa39-1d50252b510a",
                                                "text": "To melt with the sight of a smile that divulges the words unspoken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "unspoken",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0731184-5c72-3a02-8664-72f2d74da6f3",
